[{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=12x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=6-4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes.</p></li><li><p>Find the points of intersection between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the exact length of the line segment between the two points of intersection.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p1-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(6-4x)^2=12x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n36-48x+16x^2=12x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n16x^2-60x+36=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore x=\\frac34\\text{ or }x=3\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac34,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{9^2+(\\frac94)^2}=\\frac{9\\sqrt{17}}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Two curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=40x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}4+\\frac{y^2}9=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes.</p></li><li><p>Find the points of intersection between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p1-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2}4+\\frac{40x}9=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n9x^2+160x=36\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n9x^2+160x-36=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(9x-2)(x+18)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\frac29\\text{ or }x=-18\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is positive</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\frac29\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=40\\times\\frac29\\Rightarrow y=\\pm\\frac{4\\sqrt5}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(\\tfrac29,-\\tfrac{4\\sqrt5}3)\\text{ and }(\\tfrac29,\\tfrac{4\\sqrt5}3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Two curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}9-\\frac{y^2}4=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes.</p></li><li><p>Find the points of intersection between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p2-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2}9-\\frac{(-2x)}4=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4x^2+18x=36\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4x^2+18x-36=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2x^2+9x-18=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(x+6)(2x-3)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=-6\\text{ or }x=\\frac32\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is negative</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=-6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=-2\\times-6\\Rightarrow y=\\pm2\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(-6,-2\\sqrt3)\\text{ and }(-6,2\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have equations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"xy=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-kx+8\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-values of the points of intersection between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"L\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-kx+8\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a tangent to the curve.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q5-Q6: Volume of Revolution</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p3-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx(-kx+8\\sqrt2)=16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n-kx^2+8\\sqrt2x-16=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nkx^2-8\\sqrt2x+16=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore x=\\frac{8\\sqrt2\\pm\\sqrt{128-64k}}{2k}=\\frac{4\\sqrt2-4\\sqrt{2-k}}k\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-k=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A hyperbola is given by equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{3a^2}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Write down the equations of the asymptotes of the curve in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the curve.</p></li></ol><p>The finite region bounded by the curve, the positive <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Find the volume of the solid generated in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in exact form.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{3a^2}}ax=\\pm\\sqrt3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\sqrt3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p3-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{y^2}{3a^2}=\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-1\\Rightarrow y^2=3x^2-3a^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\pi\\int_a^{2a}3x^2-3a^2\\,\\mathrm dx=\\pi[x^3-3a^2x]_a^{2a}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=\\pi[(8a^3-6a^3)-(a^3-3a^3)]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=4a^3\\pi\\text{ units}^3\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>An ellipse is given by equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, sketch the curve.</p></li></ol><p>The finite region bounded by the curve, the positive <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and the positive <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis is rotated <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the volume of the solid generated in terms, giving your answer in exact form.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p4-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}{a^2}=1-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}\\Rightarrow x^2=a^2-\\frac{a^2}{b^2}y^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\pi\\int_0^ba^2-\\frac{a^2}{b^2}y^2\\,\\mathrm dy=\\pi[a^2y-\\frac{a^2}{3b^2}y^3]_0^b\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=\\pi[(a^2b-\\tfrac13a^2b)-(0)]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=\\frac23a^2b\\pi\\text{ units}^3\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A parabola <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y^2=12(x-k)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Without using Calculus, prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac3k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nm^2x^2=12x-12k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nm^2x^2-12x+12k=0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For it to be a tangent, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(-12)^2-4m^2\\times12=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n144-48m^2k=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n48m^2k=144\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nm^2=\\frac3k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore m=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac3k}\\text{ as req.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>An ellipse <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}4+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Without using Calculus, find the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2}4+\\frac{(mx+5)^2}{16}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4x^2+(mx+5)^2=16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4x^2+m^2x^2+10mx+25=16\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(4+m^2)x^2+10mx+9=0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For it to be a tangent, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(10m)^2-4(4+m^2)(9)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n100m^2-144-36m^2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n64m^2-144=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nm^2=\\frac94\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nm=-\\frac32\\text{ or }m=\\frac32\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>An ellipse <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(x-5)^2+\\frac{y^2}9=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>A second ellipse <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^2}9+(y-5)^2=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the same axes.</p></li></ol><p>A tangent line of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+y=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that this tangent line is also a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x-5)^2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(y-5)^2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.26/solutions/assets/diagrams/126-p5-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Tangent line for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(x-5)^2+\\frac{(k-x)^2}9=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n9(x-5)^2+(k-x)^2=9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n9x^2-90x+225+k^2-2kx+x^2=9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n10x^2-(90+2k)x+(216+k^2)=0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For it to be a tangent, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(-(90+2k))^2-4\\times10(216+k^2)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4k^2+360k+8100-40k^2-8640=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n-36k^2+360k-540=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nk^2-10k+15=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nk=5+\\sqrt{10}\\text{ or }k=5-\\sqrt{10}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Tangent line for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{(k-y)^2}9+(y-5)^2=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Which is the same as seen in part b) to give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10y^2-(90+2k)y+(216+k^2)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore k=5+\\sqrt{10}\\text{ or }k=5-\\sqrt{10}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the locus of points such that the distance from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is always equal to the distance from the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2=p(y+q)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found.</p>","steps":["<p>Given the general point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(x,y)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Distance to point: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{x^2+(y+4)^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Distance to line: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|y-2|\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sqrt{x^2+(y+4)^2}=|y-2|\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2+(y+4)^2=(y-2)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2+y^2+8y+16=y^2-4y+4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2=-12y-12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2=-12(y+1)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.26-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the locus of points such that the distance from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is always three times the distance from the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Given the general point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(x,y)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Distance to point: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{x^2+(y-9)^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Distance to line: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|x-1|\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sqrt{(x-9)^2+y^2}=3|x-1|\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(x-9)^2+y^2=9(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx^2-18x+81+y^2=9x^2-18x+9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny^2=8x^2-72\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n8x^2-y^2=72\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x^2}9-\\frac{y^2}{72}=1\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]